Z||000000||JetroGT||08-30-2001||04:00 PM||||I did check the other posts on clutches. That's alot of postings! <P>My car is an 87GT 5spd. Last week it woulden't start because the clutch pedal wasen't touching the switch under the dash. I had to adjust it by hand to get it to start. Then yesterday it was getting difficult to shift it into gear. I checked the tranny oil. On the stick it was below the low mark. I refilled it with syncro-mesh just now and it's still shifting hard. What gives? Bad clutch, bent pedel? Does that oil take a little driving before it works? I'm running out of ideas.<P>I'm out. Gotta go see Planet of the Apes. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by JetroGT (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||08-30-2001||04:20 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013171.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013171.html</A> <P>From a couple of days ago.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||08-30-2001||07:27 PM||||I drove it to the movies and back. It's still shifting hard. I got back and looked at the master cylinder in front. I think it's low, but I can't get the cap off. It seems like every thing that is supposed to come off, won't.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JetroGT||08-30-2001||08:01 PM||||That fixed it. their was almost no fluid in the master cylinder. I could see the bottom. Being that low it shoulde'nt have worked at all.<P><BR>||||reg||7
